Alembic migrations for the Sales Forecasting API.

The database URL is read from SCENARIO_DATABASE_URL (or DATABASE_URL) by
env.py; it is deliberately absent from alembic.ini so no credential is
committed and the same scripts run in every environment.

  alembic upgrade head          # apply
  alembic downgrade -1          # revert the last migration
  alembic current               # what is applied
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"

The API also calls create_all() at start-up, which creates missing tables but
never alters one. That exists so a fresh local database works without a
migration step; Alembic is what owns the schema anywhere it matters.
